145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 98 0 R
/T (Across these pieces, we move to moments before the market, as we now know it, emerged. Where exchange does not come from agreements between equals but rather from relations which are structured through obligation, access, and power. What appears to us as participation, reveals itself as something which was already mediated and diffused, and then further sustained through systems that no longer need to announce themselves. Within the household, reciprocity holds through expectations instead of balance, and those expectations are internalised, repeated and rarely recognised. Then we look at economies that sit at the margins, where belonging becomes necessary for survival and refusal carries hight cost. Even here exchange continues, but under conditions which violate voluntariness. In the present, as transactions are increasingly replacing continuity, what remains of exchange is its reorganisation into forms that no longer sustain what they depend on.)
/E (Across these pieces, we move to moments before the market, as we now know it, emerged. Where exchange does not come from agreements between equals but rather from relations which are structured through obligation, access, and power. What appears to us as participation, reveals itself as something which was already mediated and diffused, and then further sustained through systems that no longer need to announce themselves. Within the household, reciprocity holds through expectations instead of balance, and those expectations are internalised, repeated and rarely recognised. Then we look at economies that sit at the margins, where belonging becomes necessary for survival and refusal carries hight cost. Even here exchange continues, but under conditions which violate voluntariness. In the present, as transactions are increasingly replacing continuity, what remains of exchange is its reorganisation into forms that no longer sustain what they depend on.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 98 0 R
/T (Finally, we extend our gratitude to those who contributed, and to what made that contribution possible. What appears here is only a surface, what sustains it continues somewhere else. If there is anything to take away from this issue, it is perhaps this: what we recognise as choice is rarely where things begin and instead, is merely a point where they become visible.)
/E (Finally, we extend our gratitude to those who contributed, and to what made that contribution possible. What appears here is only a surface, what sustains it continues somewhere else. If there is anything to take away from this issue, it is perhaps this: what we recognise as choice is rarely where things begin and instead, is merely a point where they become visible.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
