1154 0 obj
<<
/Title (Entry into this system is not a simple decision. It comes into existence due to the absence of viable alternatives, and fueled by factors such as limited access to education, debt, migration, trafficking networks, and social exclusion. These are not external factors which are outside the market. They are the conditions that produce participation.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1124 0 R
/Prev 1148 0 R
/Next 1149 0 R
>>
endobj
1155 0 obj
<<
/Title (Homo Economicus only recognises labour when it is waged, measurable, exchanged; everything else is treated as outside the economy, as if it sustains itself \(which it does not\).)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1140 0 R
/Prev 1152 0 R
/Next 1153 0 R
>>
endobj
